        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level, momentum, one-off, and policy-mechanism effects: the level of 12-month CPI is still elevated at 3.4 percent, recent core momentum is closer to 0.2 percent, the latest headline downside came from energy at -1.5 percent in July, and monetary policy works slowly through demand-sensitive services rather than forcing a single-month September headline print."
