        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Upside risk is a renewed gasoline or energy-services jump plus sticky shelter, which would land above the interval if September headline CPI prints above about 0.78 percent. Downside risk is another broad energy decline or goods deflation month, which would land below the interval if the headline print is below about -0.28 percent. Outside the interval would most likely require an energy shock or a broad repricing month rather than normal core persistence."
